#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktron; is a simple Tron-Clone for the <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org\">K "
"Desktop Environment</ulink>. You can play &ktron; against the computer or a "
"friend."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The aim of the game is to live longer than your opponent. To do that, avoid "
"running into a wall, your own tail and that of your opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playing &ktron;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rules"
msgstr "Règlas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once a round is started, the players do not stop moving forward (unless the "
"game is paused). All you have to do is avoid crashing by changing your "
"players direction. Additionally you can try to hinder your opponent. For "
"this it is possible to increase the velocity by pressing your accelerator "
"key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A round starts when all human players press a direction key. The initial "
"moving direction is then in this direction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to interrupt playing, select <guimenuitem>Pause</guimenuitem> "
"from the <guimenu>Game</guimenu> menu or hit the keyboard shortcut (see "
"section <link linkend=\"keys\">Default Shortcuts</link>). Additionally the "
"game is paused when the game loses the keyboard focus, &eg; when switching "
"to an other window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To continue the game, select the menu item <guimenuitem>Pause</guimenuitem> "
"again, or the keyboard shortcut. The game will also continue if the human "
"players press one of their direction keys. But be careful, your player "
"switches to this direction immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A game consists of several rounds, and ends if a player has at least nine "
"points, and additionally two more points than the opponent. The current "
"score is always displayed in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Computer Player"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can let the computer be Player One, Player Two or both players. There "
"are three difficulty levels: Beginner, Average and Expert."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose Beginner, the computer doesn't care about the opponent and "
"just moves around. This is the same algorithm as used by xtron-1.1."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At skill levels Average and Expert, the computer tries to hinder the "
"opponent when he comes near."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See the <link linkend=\"settings-menu\"><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu</"
"link> section for information on how to configure the computer player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Keyboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each player has five keys. Four keys for changing the direction and one to "
"accelerate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The direction keys do not have to be held down. Simply press them once to "
"change the direction of your player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Acceleration only occurs while the acceleration key remains depressed. When "
"you release the acceleration key, velocity returns to normal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See section <link linkend=\"settings-menu\"><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"Menu</link> for information how to change the default keys."
msgstr ""

