#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Configuration Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting the <guimenuitem>Configure &kappname;...</guimenuitem> option in "
"the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu will open a further dialog which lets "
"you tweak &kappname;'s behavior."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid "This dialog is divided into three pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show winner by changing color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable this box to improve visualizing that the game is over by making "
"&ktron; change the color of the loser's trail to the color of the winner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disable acceleration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checking this box will disable the acceleration feature - pressing the "
"acceleration key will have no effect, both vehicles will always travel with "
"constant velocity."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "Crash when moving in the opposite direction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable this to make a vehicle crash into itself as soon as a player attempts "
"to move into the opposite direction (&ie; a vehicle moves left, and the "
"player tries to move to the right in one step). If this box is not checked, "
"nothing happens when a player attempts to move into the opposite direction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:419
#, no-c-format
msgid "Player Names"
msgstr "Noms dels jogaires"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specify custom names to use for the players to override the use of default "
"ones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speed"
msgstr "Velocitat"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this slider to define how fast the vehicles move; moving the slider to "
"the left will make the vehicles move slower, moving it to the right will "
"make them move faster."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>AI</acronym> Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Computer Controls"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use these two checkable boxes to define which players should be controlled "
"by the computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "Intelligence:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects the skill level of the computer player, <guimenuitem>Beginner</"
"guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Average</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Expert</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Beginner</guimenuitem> ignores the opponent, and just moves "
"randomly. <guimenuitem>Average</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Expert</"
"guimenuitem> causes the computer to actively hinder the opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "Appearance Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid "Line style:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can choose one of four different line styles to be used for drawing "
"the vehicles. The names of the styles are self-explanatory: <guimenuitem>3D "
"Line</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>3D Rectangles</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Flat</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Circles</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "Line Size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this slider to define how broad the trail of a vehicle should be. Moving "
"the slider towards the left will make the trail more narrow, moving it to "
"the right will result in a wider trail."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background"
msgstr "Fons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can define the appearance of the playground's background. If you "
"prefer a simple solid color, select the <guilabel>Color:</guilabel> option "
"and click on the button at the right of it to open a convenient color-"
"selection dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also choose a background image for the playground. To do so, select "
"the <guilabel>Image:</guilabel> option, and then provide the filename of a "
"wallpaper image to use in the input field at the right. Alternatively you "
"can click on the little button at the very right to open the well-known file-"
"selection dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "Player 1 color:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the colored rectangle to open a color-selection dialog which lets "
"you define the color to be used for the vehicle of the first player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "Player 2 color:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the colored rectangle to open a color-selection dialog which lets "
"you define the color to be used for the vehicle of the second player."
msgstr ""

